<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Merged into the built app's Info.plist by tauri-build.

	  Without this key macOS does not show a Bluetooth prompt at all: it kills
	  the process the moment anything touches CoreBluetooth. The failure looks
	  like a crash rather than a denied permission, which is a long way to
	  travel to find a missing string.

	  The wording is what the user reads in the system dialog, so it says what
	  the scanning is for and what it is not: the app listens for one signal
	  from one paired phone; it does not connect to anything and it does not
	  transmit.
	-->
	<key>NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Outsie 用蓝牙判断你配对的手机是否在这台 Mac 附近，以便锁屏时可以直接回车解锁。它只监听，不连接任何设备，也不发送任何信息。</string>
</dict>
</plist>
